{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And his garments</b> — four times in the Masorah: <b>ובגדיו קרועים</b> (and his garments were torn); <b>ובגדיו לא יפרום</b> (and his garments he shall not tear); <b>ובגדיו</b> (and his garments), <b>לא תשרפנה</b> (you shall not burn them). Even though a mourner is obligated in tearing, as it is written <b>ובגדיו קרועים</b> — for he mourned over the killing of Saul the anointed priest — he (the high priest) does not tear, as it is written <b>ובגדיו לא יפרום</b> (and his garments he shall not tear), for he is holy, and his garments are holy. And therefore <b>ובגדיו לא תשרפנה</b> — that the priestly garments were not burned when Nadav and Avihu were burned, according to the one who says their bodies were burned and their garments remained intact."], :book "exodus", :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :pt, :chapter 29, :timestamp "2026-07-27T13:25:29.722457753Z", :translated-from :en, :model "glm-5.2"}